WHAT AC-LWR5 BOUGHT (the R2875 orphan)
--------------------------------------
tree_snapshot shipped in R2875 with no production consumer. This suite consumes
it: the tool re-publishes a TRACKED preview pair, so the guard is exercised on a
real re-rendering body (rewrite bytes + os.utime forward), and the real tracked
pair preview/lobby-ws-report.html+.json is asserted byte- AND mtime-identical
after the whole suite runs.

HONEST BOUNDARIES
-----------------
1. This round did NOT run the socket walk: AC-LWR1..AC-LWR4 exercise the
   shipped render()/main() through synthetic evidence and a tmp publish, so the
   wire behaviour itself is still guarded only by the tool's own --check run,
   which this round did not perform. The eight LIVE readings remain unmeasured
   by the battery.
2. "Re-derive" here means the face's verdict is recomputed from its own evidence
   flags and the rendered JSON is re-counted - it is not an independent
   re-measurement of the lobby over a socket.
3. AC-LWR6 reads the matrix text and the registry source; it does not execute
   the full battery, so a future mid-list insert that shifts shards will not be
   caught by this suite.
4. Zero new payment capability: a buyer still cannot pay (no merchant id,
   server, domain, filing+ICP, miniprogram appid+secret).
5. Two more tool faces still carry no battery row this window (journey_demo and
   the rest of the carried 7 -> 6 list).
